// fantasy-nes prelude — module `nes`
//
// Cart-facing conveniences over the raw video/system natives. Registered by
// the host as an implicit import, so carts call these bare; `import nes` also
// works. Only `export`ed declarations are visible to carts.
//
// Nothing here reaches the hardware directly — every function is a wrapper
// over a native, so a cart that ignores the prelude entirely still works.
//
// STUB: two trivial exports, enough to prove the module wiring. The real
// vocabulary (color names, tile helpers, meta-sprite layout, text rendering
// into the map) is the prelude task's work.

// Master-palette index of the pure black the hardware actually produces (the
// $0F slot), which is what a cart wants for "off", not index 0. Petal has no
// hex integer literals, so master-palette indices are decimal throughout.
export let black = 15

// Pixel coordinate of a map cell's top-left corner. Carts mix pixel-space
// sprites with cell-space map writes constantly, so the conversion is worth a
// name.
export fn cell_to_px(cell)
  cell * 8
end
